  "notes": [
    "Workload: 200 requests, 150 unique prompts, 50 sent twice word for word (25%), seed 7. The repeat share is an assumption about traffic, not a measurement; cache savings scale with it.",
    "Both runs ask for anthropic/claude-opus-5-5 with max_tokens 1024, the same system prompt and 8 requests in flight. Without Dropwise every request goes straight to Bifrost; with Dropwise the same requests go through the gateway.",
    "Answers were replayed, not generated live: each prompt was sent once to anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5 on 2026-11-13 (max_tokens 1024) and both runs get that same recorded answer, whichever model the request names. Token totals therefore differ between the runs only by what Dropwise avoided; request latency includes the recorded model time.",
    "Water is estimated from measured tokens with signed registry factors, as on the receipts. Routing to a smaller model doesn't change it, because the registry has no per-model energy figure; only calls avoided and shorter answers do.",
    "Cost is a what-if: the recorded answers' measured tokens priced at list rates (USD per million tokens, 2026-11) for the model that served each call. A call kept on the large model is priced as if it had produced an answer of the same length, which is an assumption.",
    "Gateway overhead is the time a request spent inside Dropwise (classifier call, cache lookup, receipt and budget writes), excluding the model call.",
